      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is well above the maximum for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1600 mg four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 3,200 mg/day for adults in a monitored setting. Single doses are generally capped at 800 mg, and OTC use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is double the maximum daily dose. It raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** or **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (more typical for pain)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into doses\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1600 mg four times daily is intended and give the clinical reason. If you confirm it, I can enter it with a note, though pharmacy may still flag it. I can also add a note about GI prophylaxis or a duration limit."
      }
